<title>USA: Int'l Data awarded $729 mln U.S. defense contract.</title>
<headline>Int'l Data awarded $729 mln U.S. defense contract.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>International Data Products, a privately-owned computer company in Gaithersburg, Maryland, was awarded a $729 million U.S. defense contract for computers and support, the Air Force said on Friday.</p>
<p>The contract calls for delivery of some 360,000 computer systems including portables and desktops by May 2002. The award is part of the U.S. military's &quot;Desktop V&quot; procurement of computers, the Air Force said.</p>
<p>International Data officials said the award had been delayed because of an earlier protest lodged by another private company,</p>
